        "kind" : "plus#comment",
        "object" : {
          "content" : "Thanks for the help ! I&#39;ll explain<br />I&#39;ve already bought this <a href=\"http://www.ebay.in/itm/PicoPSU-90-90W-12Volt-ATX-Power-Supply-Cyncronix-/160429546791#ht_2806wt_905\" class=\"ot-anchor\">http://www.ebay.in/itm/PicoPSU-90-90W-12Volt-ATX-Power-Supply-Cyncronix-/160429546791#ht_2806wt_905</a><br /><br />This supplies all the necessary voltage outputs for the motherboard using a single 12v input. The problem is iths automatically programmed to shutdown at over 13.4v or below 10v for protection. But this happens from time to time in car. eg: during starting the engine the voltage peaks to 14v or so.<br /><br />All i need is a regulator which can provide me a fixed 12v 10A output, the LM7*** series seems to provide a constant voltage but the current is low, I just need a high current 12v regulator circuit ..sorry for the long comment :P",
          "objectType" : "comment"
        },
        "plusoners" : {
          "totalItems" : 0
        },
        "published" : "2012-02-20T19:08:21.964Z",
