        "etag" : "\"Q44G99shyMl14lSVN9oTpl4EamI/j0kqV6qkw3KIQ7tRy78AhfKL8F0\"",
        "id" : "z12ztrvonmf4wbzjp04cexrqywbvcrqgizk0k.1329767658701000",
        "kind" : "plus#comment",
        "object" : {
          "content" : "The long comment is fine -- I know exactly what you mean now. As you said, the chips that I used will not handle that current. You&#39;ll need something pretty beefy to handle that current, probably something with a heatsink. Unfortunately I don&#39;t know off the top of my head what chip you need to get it to work, but you seem to be on the right track and should be able to find what you need with some googling.",
          "objectType" : "comment",
          "originalContent" : "The long comment is fine -- I know exactly what you mean now. As you said, the chips that I used will not handle that current. You'll need something pretty beefy to handle that current, probably something with a heatsink. Unfortunately I don't know off the top of my head what chip you need to get it to work, but you seem to be on the right track and should be able to find what you need with some googling."
        },
